# SELECT50 example: UMA-S-1.1 transition-state optimization and frequencies.
#
# SETUP
# Install ORCA 6 and ORCA External Tools with UMA support as described at the
# top of job_orca.inp: https://github.com/faccts/orca-external-tools
# Replace ProgExt with the full installed oet_client path (.exe on Windows).
# Start the server in another terminal and leave it running:
#   oet_server uma -b 127.0.0.1:20001 -n 4
# Adjust the CPU allocation and cuda/cpu selection for your installation.
#
# RUN
# Use a fresh directory containing this input and a plausible TS guess named
# ts_guess.xyz (angstrom). Set the final line's charge and multiplicity.
# Run with the full path to your installed ORCA executable:
#   /path/to/orca job_orca_ts.inp > job_orca_ts.out 2>&1
# Windows PowerShell:
#   & "C:/path/to/orca.exe" job_orca_ts.inp > job_orca_ts.out 2>&1
#
# Calc_Hess/NumHess request an initial numerical Hessian for the TS search.
# NumFreq requests another frequency calculation at the optimized geometry.
# Check convergence and that the imaginary mode describes the intended reaction.
# For the companion IRC, retain the FINAL job_orca_ts.xyz and job_orca_ts.hess;
# intermediate numbered Hessians belong to earlier optimization geometries.
# This is a derived template, not an original record of a deposited TS job.
# TS keywords: https://www.faccts.de/docs/orca/6.1/manual/contents/structurereactivity/optimizations_TS.html
# Numerical Hessian: https://www.faccts.de/docs/orca/6.1/manual/contents/structurereactivity/optimizations.html
#
! ExtOpt OptTS TightOpt NumFreq

%method
  ProgExt "/path/to/oet_client"
  Ext_Params "-b 127.0.0.1:20001 --model uma-s-1p1 --task omol --device cuda"
end

%pal
  nprocs 4
end

%geom
  MaxStep 0.2
  MaxIter 1000
  Calc_Hess true
  NumHess true
end

* xyzfile 0 1 ts_guess.xyz
